  <div class="page-width">

    

      <article class="lvg-rtb-chapter">

        <div class="lvg-rtb-chapter__content">

          
            <span class="lvg-rtb-chapter__label lvg-rtb-reveal-item">
              Chapter one
            </span>
          

          
            <h2 class="lvg-rtb-reveal-item">
              It started in an operating <br>
theatre, not at a lab bench.
            </h2>
          

          <div class="lvg-rtb-chapter__columns">

            
              <div class="lvg-rtb-copy lvg-rtb-reveal-item">
                <p>In reconstructive and plastic surgery, a patient's own fat is sometimes transferred into tissue that has been damaged or structurally depleted. It is placed there to restore volume.</p>
              </div>
            

            
              <div class="lvg-rtb-copy lvg-rtb-reveal-item">
                <p>What clinicians observed over time was that the tissue around it could also improve in quality. Beyond what filling a space explains.</p><p>That observation is the origin of everything on this page. Not a claim about skincare. A question about why.</p>
              </div>
            

          </div>

        </div>

      </article>

    

      <article class="lvg-rtb-chapter">

        <div class="lvg-rtb-chapter__content">

          
            <span class="lvg-rtb-chapter__label lvg-rtb-reveal-item">
              Chapter two
            </span>
          

          
            <h2 class="lvg-rtb-reveal-item">
              The cells were talking <br>
to the tissue around them.
            </h2>
          

          <div class="lvg-rtb-chapter__columns">

            
              <div class="lvg-rtb-copy lvg-rtb-reveal-item">
                <p>Research into adipose tissue identified regenerative cell populations living in it, and showed that a substantial part of their effect on neighbouring tissue comes from what they release rather than from what they become.</p>
              </div>
            

            
              <div class="lvg-rtb-copy lvg-rtb-reveal-item">
                <p>Cultured under controlled conditions, those cells release proteins and other signalling substances into the medium around them. Collect that medium, process it, and remove the cells: what is left is conditioned media.</p>
              </div>
            

          </div>

        </div>

      </article>

    

  </div>
